{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Wing_Statue","to":"Wing Statue"},{"from":"Match_and_Keep","to":"Match and Keep"},{"from":"The_Mausoleum","to":"The Mausoleum"},{"from":"A_Note_For_Yourself","to":"A Note For Yourself"},{"from":"Sensory_Stone","to":"Sensory Stone"},{"from":"Hypnotizing_Colored_Mushrooms","to":"Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms"},{"from":"Mind_Bloom","to":"Mind Bloom"},{"from":"We_Meet_Again!","to":"We Meet Again!"},{"from":"Big_Fish","to":"Big Fish"},{"from":"Ancient_Writing","to":"Ancient Writing"},{"from":"Shining_Light","to":"Shining Light"},{"from":"Scrap_Ooze","to":"Scrap Ooze"},{"from":"The_Ssssserpent","to":"The Ssssserpent"},{"from":"Pleading_Vagrant","to":"Pleading Vagrant"},{"from":"World_of_Goop","to":"World of Goop"},{"from":"Dead_Adventurer","to":"Dead Adventurer"},{"from":"The_Moai_Head","to":"The Moai Head"}],"pages":{"2385":{"pageid":2385,"ns":0,"title":"A Note For Yourself","revisions":[{"revid":55257,"parentid":54537,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=A Note For Yourself\n|Image=Event-SelfNote.png\n}}\n{{E|A Note For Yourself}} is an [[Event]] encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Take and Give}} {{TS|positive||Receive and Store a Card}}\n* Receive a card that you had stored previously, and store a card in your deck in return.\n** The first time the player encounters this event in their save file, it will have {{C|Iron Wave}} stored.\n{{Frame|Ignore}} Nothing happens.\n<br>\n<br>\nYou are then given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>You spot a loose brick within a pillar that catches your eye.</i><br>\n<i>You find a folded note and a {{TS|gold||card}} inside. It reads,</i><br>\n\"The Heart awaits\"<br><br>\n<i>This is your handwriting.</i><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Take and Give}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>Choose a Card to Store.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\nPrior to {{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>\"What is going on?\"</i>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n== Gameplay Notes ==\n* This event can store a card between runs, and allows the player to obtain a card from a different character.\n* On {{Asc|14}} or lower, the player must have beaten that Ascension level on the chosen character in order to encounter this event. \n* On {{Asc|15}} or higher, this event cannot be encountered.\n* Playing the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] also disables this event.\n* If you store an upgraded card, it remains upgraded when found on another run.\n** {{C|Searing Blow}} retains its upgrade level when it was stored.\n* Retrieving a card is considered adding a card to your deck, and will trigger relics such as {{R|Molten Egg}}, {{R|Toxic Egg}}, {{R|Frozen Egg}}, and {{R|Ceramic Fish}}.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3201":{"pageid":3201,"ns":0,"title":"Ancient Writing","revisions":[{"revid":55303,"parentid":54574,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Ancient Writing\n|Image=Event-AncientWriting.png\n}}\n{{E|Ancient Writing}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Elegance}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Simplicity}} {{TS|positive||[[Upgrade]] all Strikes and Defends.}}\n* Only includes {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} cards.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nScaling the city, you notice a wall covered in the writing of {{TS|gold|up|Ancients.}} As you try to wrap your head around what the puzzling symbols and glyphs could mean, the writing begins to {{TS|blue|up|glow.}}<br>\nSuddenly, the message becomes clear...\n</div>\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Elegance}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe answer was elegance.<br>\nOf course.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Simplicity}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe truth is always simple.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The internal name of this event is <code>Back_to_Basics</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fixed softlock caused if you can't remove cards in: Back to Basics, Cleric, and Living Wall events.\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Ascender's Bane can no longer be removed by Back to Basics event.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"1846":{"pageid":1846,"ns":0,"title":"Big Fish","revisions":[{"revid":55390,"parentid":54535,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Big Fish\n|Image=Event-BigFish.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Regret}}\n{{E|Big Fish}} is an event found exclusively in [[Act 1]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Banana}} {{TS|positive||Heal 1/3 of your max HP.}}\n* If the player's HP is not divisble by 3, the HP gain is rounded down.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Donut}} {{TS|positive||Max HP +5.}}\n* Like all HP gain, the extra hit points are healed when you get them.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Box}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a [[Relic]].}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed - {{C|Regret}}.}}\n* The {{QueryLink|Relics||Relic}} is a randomly selected {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, or {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} Relic.\n<br>\nYou are then given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">As you make your way down a long corridor you see a {{TS|gold||banana}}, a {{TS|gold||donut}}, and a {{TS|gold||box}} {{TS||up|floating}} about. No... upon closer inspection they are tied to strings coming from holes in the ceiling. There is a quiet {{TS||shake|cackling}} from above as you approach the objects.\nWhat do you do?\n</div>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Banana}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou eat the {{TS|gold||banana}}. It is nutritious and slightly {{TS|blue||magical}}, healing you.</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Donut}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou eat the {{TS|gold||donut}}. It really hits the spot! Your Max HP increases.</div>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Box}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou grab the box. Inside you find a {{TS|gold||relic!}}<br>\nHowever, you really craved the donut...<br>\nYou are filled with {{TS||up|sadness,}} but mostly <span class=\"negative-text\">regret</span>.</div>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3203":{"pageid":3203,"ns":0,"title":"Dead Adventurer","revisions":[{"revid":55412,"parentid":54551,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Dead Adventurer\n|Image=Event-DeadAdventurer.png\n}}\n{{E|Dead Adventurer}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 1]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Search}} {{TS|positive||Find Loot.}} {{TS|negative||25%}} {{Asc|15|(35%)}}{{TS|negative||: monster returns.}}\n* Each {{Frame|Search}} attempt will either cause an [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Act 1 Elite]] to return and fight the player, or yield one of the following rewards:\n** 30 [[Gold]]\n** A random [[Relic]]\n** Nothing\n* Each reward only occurs once - if the player's first search found nothing and the second search found the [[Relic]], the third search will either reward 30 [[Gold]] or start a battle.\n* Each reward that is acquired before fighting the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] will be removed from its combat rewards if the player eventually does fight the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] and defeats it.\n** For example, if the player's first {{Frame|Search}} is a [[Relic]], the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] will not drop a [[Relic]] when it is defeated.\n** This is also the reason why this specific [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] fight can drop 30 extra [[Gold]] compared to a normal [[Elite]]; because the 30 [[Gold]] {{Frame|Search}} reward is added to the normal [[Gold]] reward of defeating an [[Elite]].\n* Each subsequent {{Frame|Search}} increases the chance to encounter an [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] by 25%.\n* If the player manages to successfully {{Frame|Search}} three times without encountering an  [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]], the event will end with a short dialogue detailing the success.\n* For the second and third searches (assuming the player is not ambushed), {{Frame|Search}} will be called {{Frame|Continue}} instead. Its behavior and description are unchanged.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou come across a {{TS|negative||dead adventurer}} on the floor.<br>\nHis {{TS|blue||pants}} have been stolen! Also, <code>(phrasing depends on the Elite)</code>.<br>\nThough his {{TS|gold||possessions are still intact,}} you're in no mind to find out what happened here...\n</div><br><br>\n\nThe phrasing on how the adventurer died depends on which [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] will be fought if a {{Frame|Search}} attempt fails:\n* '''For {{M|Gremlin Nob}}:''' <i>Also, it looks as though he's been {{TS|negative|shake|gouged and trampled}} by a horned beast.</i>\n* '''For {{M|Sentry|Sentries}}:''' <i>Also, the armor and face appear to be {{TS|negative|shake|scoured by flames.}}</i>\n* '''For {{M|Lagavulin}}:''' <i>Also, he looks to have been {{TS|negative|shake|eviscerated and chopped}} by giant claws.</i>\n** {{M|Lagavulin}} during this event is particularly dangerous as it '''does not''' enter combat {{Int|Lagavulin|Sleep|Asleep}}. It also immediately debuffs the player with its {{Int|Lagavulin|Siphon Soul}} on the first turn of the fight.\n<br>\n\n{{Frame|Search}} (and {{Frame|Continue}} for the second and third searches)\n<blockquote>\nIf the player finds [[Gold]]:\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou found some {{TS|gold||gold!}}<br>\nContinue searching?\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to {{Frame|Continue}} searching with a +25% chance for the monster to return, or {{Frame|Leave}} and end the event.\n</blockquote>\n\nIf the player finds a [[Relic]]:\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou found a {{TS|gold||relic!}}<br>\nContinue searching?\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to {{Frame|Continue}} searching with a +25% chance for the monster to return, or {{Frame|Leave}} and end the event.\n</blockquote>\n\nIf the player finds nothing:\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nHmm, couldn't find anything...<br>\nContinue searching?\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to {{Frame|Continue}} searching with a +25% chance for the monster to return, or {{Frame|Leave}} and end the event.\n</blockquote>\n\nIf the player is ambushed by the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]]:\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">While searching the adventurer you are caught off guard!</div>\n\n{{Frame|Fight}}\n\nThe player enters a fight with the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]]. The event ends with no additional dialogue after the [[Elites#Act 1 Elites|Elite]] is defeated.\n</blockquote>\n\nIf this is the third successful Search in a row:\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">Looks like you searched all his belongings without a hitch!</div>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n\nThe event ends with no additional dialogue.\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou exit without a sound.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Black Star}} will not cause the [[Elite]] to drop an additional [[Relic]]. However, the other \"elite relics\" {{R|Preserved Insect}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, and {{R|Slaver's Collar}} will work as expected.\n* It is quite unlikely for the player to be able to {{Frame|Search}} three times without being ambushed since they must succeed on all three searches with increasing chances of failure. See the table below for more information:\n<!-- (1 - 0.25) * (1 - 0.5) * (1 - 0.75),   OR   (1 - 0.35) * (1 - 0.6) * (1 - 0.85) -->\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+ Cumulative Chance of Avoiding the Elite\n|-\n! Number of Searches<br>(% chance of Elite returning) !! Before {{Asc|15}} !! {{Asc|15}} and Above\n|-\n| 1 (25% / {{Asc|15|35%}}) || 75% || 65%\n|-\n| 2 (50% / {{Asc|15|60%}}) || 37.5% || 26%\n|-\n| 3 (75% / {{Asc|15|85%}}) || 9.375% || 3.9%\n|}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The image of the dead adventurer is called <code>nopants.png</code> internally.\n* {{E|Dead Adventurer}} is one of three possible ways to fight an [[Elite]] outside of an [[Map Locations#Elites|Elite floor]]; the others being {{E|The Colosseum}} (with {{M|Taskmaster}} and {{M|Gremlin Nob}}) and the [[Spheric_Guardian#Act_2|Act 2 fight]] with one {{M|Sentry}} and a {{M|Spheric Guardian}}.\n* {{E|Dead Adventurer}}'s {{M|Lagavulin}} is the only case where an [[Elite]] enemy has different behavior compared to its typical encounter on an [[Map Locations#Elites|Elite floor]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Fixed Dead Adventurer event was not giving the gold correctly (just showing the effect).\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Preserved Insect and Sling should now work in all elite combats including elite battles from events (like dead adventurer event).\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Minor dialog improvement for Dead Adventurer event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Gold gain effect from things like Dead Adventurer is now a localizeable string.\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Fixed a new line character placed incorrectly for dead adventurer's event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Dead Adventurer event can now only appear on floor 7 and above.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3059":{"pageid":3059,"ns":0,"title":"Duplicator","revisions":[{"revid":54539,"parentid":35706,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Duplicator\n|Image=Event-Duplicator.png\n}}\n{{E|Duplicator}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than normal events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{TS|positive||Duplicate a card in your deck.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nBefore you lies a decorated altar to some ancient entity.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou kneel respectfully. A ghastly mirror image appears from the shrine and collides into you.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou ignore the shrine, confident in your choice.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3172":{"pageid":3172,"ns":0,"title":"Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms","revisions":[{"revid":54553,"parentid":35655,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms\n|Image=Event-Mushrooms.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Odd Mushroom}} {{Small Card Infobox|Parasite}}\n{{E|Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms}} is an [[Event]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It will only appear if the player is on floor 7 or above. This Event is the only way to obtain {{R|Odd Mushroom}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Stomp}} {{TS|negative||Anger the Mushrooms.}}<br>\n* Enter a battle against 3 {{M|Fungi Beast|Fungi Beasts}}. Winning grants the exclusive [[Relic]] {{R|Odd Mushroom}} along with regular combat rewards.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Eat}} {{TS|positive||Heal X HP.}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Parasite}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n* X is equal to 25% of the player's max HP.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou enter a corridor full of {{TS|blue|up|hypnotizing colored mushrooms.}}\n<br>\nDue to your lack of specialization in mycology you are unable to identify the specimens.\n<br>\nYou want to escape, but feel oddly compelled to eat a {{TS|blue|up|mushroom...}}\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Stomp}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|negative|shake|Ambushed!!}}\n<br>\nRodents infested by the mushrooms appear out of nowhere!\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Eat}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou give in to the unnatural desire to eat. As you consume mushroom after mushroom, you feel yourself entering into a daze and pass out. As you awake, you feel very odd. You {{TS|green||Heal}} {{TS|blue||25%}} of your HP, but you also get {{TS|negative||infected.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This Event features unique graphics of mushrooms sprouting out of the floor in the background and foreground, as seen below.\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:row; gap:10px; margin:0 0 10px 10px;\">\n[[File:BgShrooms.png|200px|thumb|Background.]][[File:FgShrooms.png|200px|thumb|Foreground.]]\n</div>\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Mushroom event now correctly shows card preview for Parasite curse.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3061":{"pageid":3061,"ns":0,"title":"Lab","revisions":[{"revid":54541,"parentid":35670,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Lab\n|Image=Event-Lab.png\n}}\n{{E|Lab}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Search}} {{TS|positive||Find some Potions!}}\n* Opens a rewards menu with three ({{Asc|15|two}}) random [[Potions]]. These can be skipped.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><i>\nYou find yourself in a room filled with racks of test tubes, beakers, flasks, forceps, pinch clamps, stirring rods, tongs, goggles funnels, pipets, cylinders, condensers, and even a rare spiral tube of glass. <br>\n\nWhy do you know the names of all these tools? It doesn't matter, you take a look around.\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3062":{"pageid":3062,"ns":0,"title":"Match and Keep","revisions":[{"revid":54542,"parentid":35675,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Match and Keep\n|Image=Event-MatchAndKeep.png\n}}\n{{E|Match and Keep}} is a shrine [[Event]] encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Play}} \n* Play a matching game for cards. Match pairs of cards to add them to your deck. There is always a pair of one {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card and one {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nA gremlin is madly shuffling cards on a table. This monster seems to be a harmless one. You approach him out of curiosity.\n</div>\n\nBefore selecting {{Frame|Play}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"{{TS|blue||Twelve}} cards! Match them to keep them! {{TS|blue||Five}} tries, no do-overs. <br>\nAre you ready? Let's start!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\nAfter {{Frame|Play}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou complete the gremlin's game and look up. <br>\nHe disappeared?\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3187":{"pageid":3187,"ns":0,"title":"Mind Bloom","revisions":[{"revid":55444,"parentid":54567,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Mind Bloom\n|Image=Event-MindBloom.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Mark of the Bloom}} {{Small Card Infobox|Normality}} {{Small Card Infobox|Doubt}}\n{{E|Mind Bloom}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|I am War}} {{TS|negative||Fight a [[Bosses#Act 1 Bosses|Boss]] from Act 1.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].}}\n* The boss is selected at random. It can be the same boss that the player actually fought in [[Act 1]], or one of the two that they did not encounter.\n* In addition to the Boss dropping a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]], it also drops normal combat rewards and 50 {{Asc|15|(25)}} [[Gold]].\n<br>\n{{Frame|I am Awake}} {{TS|positive||[[Upgrade]] all cards.}} {{TS|negative||You can no longer heal.}}\n* Obtain {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n<br>\n{{Frame|I am Rich}} {{TS|positive||Gain 999 [[Gold]].}} {{TS|negative||Cursed - 2 {{C|Normality}}.}}\n* This option only appears on floors 35 to 40.\n<br>\n{{Frame|I am Healthy}} {{TS|positive||Heal to full HP.}} {{TS|negative||Cursed - {{C|Doubt}}.}}\n* This option replaces {{Frame|I am Rich}} on floor 41 and above.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nWhile walking and traversing through the chaos of the Spire, your thoughts suddenly begin to feel very... {{TS|purple|up|real...}}<br>\n\nImaginings of {{TS|red||monsters}} and {{TS|gold||riches}} begin to manifest themselves into reality.<br>\nThe sensation is quickly fleeting. What do you do?\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|I am War}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue; the player immediately enters combat with the random [[Bosses#Act 1 Bosses|Boss from Act 1]])\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|I am Awake}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nEverything makes sense now.<br>\nThe lack of memories, the ascent, the {{TS|gold||Ancient One.}}<br>\n\nThis is the way it always was.<br>\nThis is the way it always will be.<br>\nAll will be forgotten again soon...\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|I am Rich}} or {{Frame|I am Healthy}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nCan it really be this easy?\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Because the healing prevention of {{Frame|I am Awake}} is implemented as the {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} relic, it can disqualify the player from the [[Achievements|''Who Needs Relics?'' achievement]].\n* The boss fight from {{Frame|I am War}} will trigger {{R|Pantograph}} and {{R|Slaver's Collar}} as if it were a normal end-of-Act boss fight.\n* {{R|Omamori}} can prevent one or both {{C|Normality}} curses from {{Frame|I am Rich}} if it has one or both uses remaining. This allows the player to receive 999 [[Gold]] with practically no downside, especially considering that {{E|Mind Bloom}} is often one of the last opportunities to encounter {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} in a run.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The boss music that plays during the {{Frame|I am War}} fight is a slightly different version of the normal Act 1 Boss music (''The Guardian Emerges'') simply called ''Mind Bloom'' in the Slay the Spire Original Soundtrack.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Bottled Cards upgraded from Mind Bloom event have their description updated correctly.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Because new music was added into the game, it is now also available in our Official Soundtrack. Newly added tracks include: Mind Bloom\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Mind Bloom event combat now correctly gives appropriate gold for the battle.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 43: Discovery'''\n** Mind Bloom event now correctly shows curse previews for its event options.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding special BGM when fighting a boss via Mind Bloom event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Fixed an incorrect interaction with Mark of the Bloom and the Moai Head event in Act 3.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Mind Bloom event's boss battle no longer counts as a boss for scoring or achievements.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** Mind Bloom no longer shows status/curse cards upgrading.\n** Mind Bloom upgrade now only shows up to 20 cards as it's CPU intensive.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** New Act 3 event: Mind Bloom\n** New Relic: Mark of the Bloom\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3180":{"pageid":3180,"ns":0,"title":"Pleading Vagrant","revisions":[{"revid":55476,"parentid":54581,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Pleading Vagrant\n|Image=Event-Vagrant.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Shame}}\n{{E|Pleading Vagrant}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It will only appear if the player has at least 75 [[Gold]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Offer Gold}} {{TS|gold||85 [[Gold]]:}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a [[Relic]].}}\n* If the player does not have enough [[Gold]], this option will be greyed out.\n\n{{Frame|Rob}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a [[Relic]].}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Shame}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nWhile sneaking past a group of shrouded figures, one of them approaches you.\n<br>\n\"Got anything for me friend? Please... maybe some {{TS|gold||Coin?\"}}\n<br>\n\"I just need somewhere to stay, I have treasures I can trade...\"\n<br>\nHe seems delusional, but harmless.\n</div>\n<br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Offer Gold}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Oh yes, {{TS||up|yes!}} Here here, a fair trade!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Rob}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou snatch the precious {{TS|gold||relic}} from his clutches and walk away.\n<br>\nFrom behind you hear,\n<br>\n\"Have you no shame? {{TS||up|HAVE YOU NO SHAAAAAME?!\"}}\n<br>\nYou have some {{TS|purple||shame.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue)\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Omamori}} can be used to prevent the {{C|Shame}} from {{Frame|Rob}} if it has any charges remaining.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Pleading Vagrant Event was originally called \"Addicted\". It was renamed because, early into Slay the Spire's development, the vagrant previously accepted {{C|J.A.X.}} from the {{E|Augmenter}} event but was reworked to accept 85 [[Gold]] instead. Following the change, the old name no longer made sense and had to also be changed. It could have also been changed due to the negative connotations and implication of substance abuse.\n* Internally called <code>Addict</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 45: Impatience'''\n** Some events like Pleading Vagrant did not correctly remove remaining event choices when selecting the leave option.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Typo Fix on Pleading Vagrant event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Addict event reworked.\n** Addicted event renamed -> Pleading Vagrant.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3064":{"pageid":3064,"ns":0,"title":"Purifier","revisions":[{"revid":54543,"parentid":35683,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Purifier\n|Image=Event-Purifier.png\n}}\n{{E|Purifier}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events occur less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i> Before you lies an elaborate shrine to a forgotten spirit. </i>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote>\n<i> As you kneel in reverence, you feel a weight lifted off your shoulders.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\n<i> You ignore the shrine. </i>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* This probably would not work as an air purifier.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3164":{"pageid":3164,"ns":0,"title":"Scrap Ooze","revisions":[{"revid":54555,"parentid":35659,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Scrap Ooze\n|Image=Event-ScrapOoze.png\n}}\n{{E|Scrap Ooze}} is an event found exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Reach Inside}} {{TS|negative||Lose 3}} {{Asc|15|(5)}} {{TS|negative||HP.}} {{TS|positive||25% chance to find a [[Relic]].}}\n* If you fail to find a [[Relic]], you can try again until you find one. Each time you fail, the HP loss is increased by 1 and the chance to gain a Relic increases by 10%.\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Relic Distribution ==\n* {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common Relics}} - 17% chance\n* {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon Relics}} - 33% chance\n* {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare Relics}} - 50% chance\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you walk into the room you hear a {{TS||up|gurgling}} and the {{TS||shake|grinding}} of metals. Before you is a slime-like creature that ate too much scrap for its own good. From the center of the creature you see glints of strange light, perhaps something magical? It looks like you can get some {{TS|gold||treasure}} if you just reach inside its... opening. However, the acid and sharp objects may {{TS|negative||hurt.}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Reach Inside}}\n<blockquote>\nFound Nothing\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|negative|shake|Ouch!}} <br>\nAll you find is corroded metal and a bit of {{TS|negative|shake|burning pain.}} <br>\nHowever, you're still convinced there's a {{TS|gold||relic...}} <br>\n</div></blockquote>\n\nFound a Relic\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|positive||Success!}} <br>\nAfter rummaging through the metal and burning acid, you finally grab hold of a {{TS|gold||relic}} and yank it out. <br>\nYou pull your way out of the ooze {{TS|negative||damaged}} but rewarded.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou decide to leave the area. <br>\nThe slime pays no attention, content with its meal.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n<!--\nBe careful with the math in this table if you plan on rewriting this section! Cumulative probability can be tricky and unintuitive.\nThe chance for having found the relic by this attempt or earlier is: 1 - ((1-A) * (1-B) * (1-C) * ...)\nwhere A, B, C, etc. are the subsequent \"Chance of Finding the Relic on This Attempt\".\n\nFor example, there is a ~73.19% chance to have found the relic after your third attempt.\nThe math is: 1 - ((1-0.25) * (1-0.35) * (1-0.45)) = 1 - (0.75 * 0.65 * 0.55) = 1 - 0.268125 = 0.731875 ~= 73.19%\n\nAnother way to think about it is to find the chance that we HAVEN'T found the relic by this attempt (e.g. (1 - the 25% chance to find it on Attempt #1) = 75% chance to NOT find it on Attempt #1),\nand then the inverse of that (1 - the final % after multiplying them all together) is the chance that we HAVE found the relic by that attempt.\n-->\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+ Scrap Ooze Details and Math\n|-\n! Number of Attempts !! HP Lost on This Attempt !! Chance of Finding the [[Relic]]<br>on This Attempt !! Total HP Lost !! Chance of Having Found the [[Relic]]<br>by This Attempt (i.e. Cumulative Chance)\n|-\n| 1 || 3 ({{Asc|15|5}}) || 25% || 3 ({{Asc|15|5}}) || 25%\n|-\n| 2 || 4 ({{Asc|15|6}}) || 35% || 7 ({{Asc|15|11}}) || 51.25%\n|-\n| 3 || 5 ({{Asc|15|7}}) || 45% || 12 ({{Asc|15|18}}) || ~73.19%\n|-\n| 4 || 6 ({{Asc|15|8}}) || 55% || 18 ({{Asc|15|26}}) || ~87.93%\n|-\n| 5 || 7 ({{Asc|15|9}}) || 65% || 25 ({{Asc|15|35}}) || ~95.78%\n|-\n| 6 || 8 ({{Asc|15|10}}) || 75% || 33 ({{Asc|15|45}}) || ~98.94%\n|-\n| 7 || 9 ({{Asc|15|11}}) || 85% || 42 ({{Asc|15|56}}) || ~99.84%\n|-\n| 8 || 10 ({{Asc|15|12}}) || 95% || 52 ({{Asc|15|68}}) || ~99.99%\n|-\n| 9 || 11 ({{Asc|15|13}}) || 105% (100%) || 63 ({{Asc|15|81}}) || 100%\n\n|}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Events: Falling, Secret Portal, Knowing Skull, Golden Idol, and Scrap Ooze receive ambient BGM.\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Seeds utilized for several events for consistent outcomes: Accursed Blacksmith, Cursed Tome, Scrap Ooze, N'loth.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Wording improvements to Scrap Ooze event.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Scrap Ooze event wording improved for added clarity.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3191":{"pageid":3191,"ns":0,"title":"Sensory Stone","revisions":[{"revid":55936,"parentid":55494,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Sensory Stone\n|Image=Event-SensoryStone.png\n}}\n{{E|Sensory Stone}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]]. \n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Recall}} {{TS|positive||Add 1 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card to your deck.}}\n\n{{Frame|Recall}} {{TS|positive||Add 2 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards to your deck.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 5 HP.}}\n\n{{Frame|Recall}} {{TS|positive||Add 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards to your deck.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 10 HP.}}\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>Navigating through the Beyond, you discover a {{TS|blue||glowing tesseract}} {{TS||shake|spinning}} and {{TS||up|shifting}} gently in the air.</i><br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Interact}}\n<br>\n<br>\n<i>You touch it.</i><br>\n<br>\n<i>\nA {{TS|negative|shake|sharp pain}} flows through you, followed by vivid flashes of a distant memory.<br>\n...whose memories are these?\n</i><br>\n<br>\n\n{{Frame|Recall}}\n\nAfter leaving the card rewards screen, the player is presented with one of four possible dialogue texts. Each contains the memories of one of the four playable characters. The dialogue is chosen randomly, and the current character being played has no effect on which one is presented.<br>\n<br>\n'''[[Ironclad]]'s Memories'''\n<blockquote><i>\n{{TS|red|up|FEAR.}}<br>\n\nA demonic creature towers above you, wings spread wide as it howls with laughter. Dead bodies of a tribe surround you while the village is engulfed in terrible {{TS|purple|up|dark flames.}}<br>\n\nThe demon calls out, taunting you.<br>\n\n\" {{TS|red|shake|YOU REALLY ARE THE STRONGEST NOW! Haha.. HEHE... HAHAHAAAAH!!}} \"<br> <!-- There actually are spaces between the \" and the text in-game -->\n\nThis laughter echoes forever...\n</i></blockquote>\n\n'''[[Silent]]'s Memories'''\n<blockquote><i>\n{{TS|green|up|TRIUMPH.}}<br>\n\nThe remains of a {{TS|purple|up|ghostly creature}} sink slowly into the mud before you, barely visible in the moonlight. You have proven yourself amongst your sisters.<br>\n\nStanding victoriously, you wait in silence as the others ceremoniously place the {{TS|gold||creature's skull}} atop your head. The ritual has concluded.<br>\n\nYou head towards the Spire...\n</i></blockquote>\n\n'''[[Defect]]'s Memories'''\n<blockquote><i>\n{{TS|blue|up|CONFUSION.}}<br>\n\n{{TS|gold||[OBJECTIVE]}} {{TS|green||BALANCE must be ENFORCED}}<br>\n{{TS|gold||[DEFINE]}} {{TS|green||BALANCE}}<br>\n{{TS|gold||[ERROR]}} {{TS|green||BALANCE NOT FOUND}}<br>\n{{TS|gold||[DEFINE]}} {{TS|green||BALANCE}}<br>\n{{TS|gold||[ERROR]}} {{TS|green||BALANCE NOT FOUND}}<br>\n{{TS|gold||[WARNING]}} {{TS|red||Large object approaching}}<br>\n\n{{TS||up|\"I... ..am ....Neow..\"}}\n</i></blockquote>\n\n'''[[Watcher]]'s Memories'''\n<blockquote><i>\n{{TS|purple|up|SERENITY.}}<br>\n\nTwo primitive creatures fight over a carcass on the side of the road. You observe, devoid of emotion.<br>\n{{TS|gold||Watch. Remember. Live.}} This is the Watcher's mission.<br>\n\nRecently, one of your peers had stopped reporting on their assignment: a Spire of unknown origin.<br>\n\nAs the fight ends, you continue onward, unfazed by the bloody scene that took place.\n</i></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Since the {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless cards}} are actually card rewards, they are affected by [[Relics]] which modify card rewards in some way.\n** {{R|Question Card}} makes each card reward present the player with 1 additional card.\n** {{R|Singing Bowl}} can allow the player to skip each card reward in order to gain +2 Max HP.\n** {{R|Busted Crown}} makes each card reward present the player with 2 fewer cards.\n** {{R|N'loth's Gift}} increases the likelihood of each card being a {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare&color:Colorless|Rare Colorless card}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* [[Ironclad]]'s {{TS|red|up|FEAR}} memory may be a reference to his {{C|Demon Form}} card as it depicts his increased power through his {{C|Burning Pact}} with a demon.\n** {{KW2|Vakuu}} is most likely the demonic creature in Ironclad's memory, it possibly takes place directly after the Epoch, {{2|Timeline#Devastation|Devastation}}.\n* [[Silent]]'s {{TS|green|up|TRIUMPH}} memory may be a reference to her {{C|Wraith Form}} card as it depicts the end of her fight against a \"ghostly creature\".\n** It is also likely the origin of her iconic skull mask.\n** It may also reference {{M|Nemesis}}; the \"ghostly creature\" could match the behaviour where the monster gains {{BD|Intangible}} while fighting it. Its green rags may be somewhat reminiscent of the cloak that [[Silent]] wears as well. \"Nemesis\" is also a somewhat odd name for a monster as a \"nemesis\" can also be interpreted as an \"[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archenemy archenemy]\"; the main enemy of a protagonist.\n* [[Defect]]'s {{TS|blue|up|CONFUSION}} memory may be a reference to its self-aware nature, perhaps triggered by its inability to define or understand \"balance\", before being found by [[Neow]].\n* [[Watcher]]'s {{TS|purple|up|SERENITY}} memory may be a reference to {{E|The Joust}} as she watches two knights fight over the remains of \"Noodles\"; the former pet of one of the knights.\n** It is also [[Time Eater#Trivia|one of the hints]] that may indicate that {{M|Time Eater}} used to belong to Watcher's order as it is possible that they were the peer who entered the Spire and never returned.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** ''NOTE: There are no official patch notes for this change, but the Sensory Stone event gained its fourth dialogue option memory for the Watcher.''\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient SFX for Sensory Stone event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** Fix grammar issue in Sensory Stone event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Additional lore in the Sensory Stone event.\n** Egg relics now show pre-upgraded cards for Sensory Stone event's choices.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Sensory Stone event wording fix.\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Wording fixes in Sensory Stone event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** Grammar improvements for Sensory Stone event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Hotfix: Fixed issue where Sensory Stone event may give you colored cards.\n** New Event (Beyond): Sensory Stone.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3173":{"pageid":3173,"ns":0,"title":"Shining Light","revisions":[{"revid":54556,"parentid":35660,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Shining Light\n|Image=Event-ShiningLight.png\n}}\n{{E|Shining Light}} is an [[Event]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Enter}} {{TS|positive||Upgrade 2 random cards.}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 20% {{Asc|15|(30%)}} of the player's max HP.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou find a shimmering {{TS|gold||mass of light}} encompassing the center of the room.\n<br>\nIts {{TS||up|warm glow}} and {{TS||up|enchanting patterns}} invite you in.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Enter}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you walk through the light, you notice that the light is absorbed into you.\n<br>\nIt's {{TS|negative|shake|scorching hot}} ! However, the pain quickly recedes.\n<br>\nYou feel {{TS|blue||invigorated,}} as though you received a well deserved slap.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou walk around it, wondering what could have been.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Cards from Shining Light event are now positioned correctly.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3181":{"pageid":3181,"ns":0,"title":"The Mausoleum","revisions":[{"revid":55458,"parentid":54584,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Mausoleum\n|Image=Event-Mausoleum.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Writhe}}\n{{E|The Mausoleum}} is an [[Event]] found in [[Act 2]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Open Coffin}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a [[Relic]].}} {{TS|negative||50% {{Asc|15|(100%)}}: Become Cursed - {{C|Writhe}}}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nVenturing through a series of tombs, you are faced with a large sarcophagus {{TS||up|studded with gems}} in the center of a circular room. <br>\nYou cannot make out the writing on the coffin, however, you do notice {{TS|purple|up|black fog}} seeping out from the sides.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Open Coffin}}\n\nThe dialogue changes depending on whether the player becomes cursed with {{C|Writhe}} or not.\n\n'''If the player does not receive {{C|Writhe}}:'''\n\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou push open the coffin. The fog dissipates harmlessly. Inside, you find the mortal remains of a decorated soldier grasping an old {{TS|gold||relic.}} You pilfer it and move on.\n</div>\n</blockquote>\n\n'''If the player receives {{C|Writhe}}:'''\n\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou push open the coffin. As you do, {{TS|purple|up|black fog}} spews forth and covers the entire room! Inside, you find no body, only a {{TS|gold|up|relic.}} You take it and move onwards, {{TS|negative|shake|coughing violently.}}\n</div>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou continue on your way, leaving the forgotten dead undisturbed.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n<!-- I originally didn't trust this information from the Fandom wiki, but I confirmed it was correct using Basemod to repeatedly enter the event and claim the relic until it yielded Matryoshka and Darkstone Periapt -->\n* If the player receives {{R|Omamori}} as the [[Relic]] reward, it '''will not''' prevent the {{C|Writhe}} from being gained.\n* If the player receives {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} as the [[Relic]] reward, it '''will''' grant the +6 Max HP.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum mausoleum] is a building that encloses and protects the burial chamber of one or more deceased. The term \"mausoleum\" comes from the burial chamber of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausolus King Mausolus] as enclosed by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_at_Halicarnassus Mausoleum at Halicarnassus].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient SFX for Mausoleum event. \n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Seeds are now utilized for The Mausoleum event.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3174":{"pageid":3174,"ns":0,"title":"The Moai Head","revisions":[{"revid":55511,"parentid":54570,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Moai Head\n|Image=Event-MoaiHead.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Golden Idol}}\n{{E|The Moai Head}} is an [[Event]] found in [[Act 3]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}. It can only be encountered if the player either has {{R|Golden Idol}}, or their HP is at or below 50%.\n\n== Options ==\n<!-- Fix descriptions to be game-accurate. Use TS colors for positive and negative effects. Put any extra information in indented bullet points. -->\n{{Frame|Jump Inside}} {{TS|positive||Heal to full HP.}} {{TS|negative||Lose X Max HP.}}\n* X is equal to 12.5% {{Asc|15|(18%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Offer: {{R|Golden Idol}}}} {{TS|positive||Receive 333 [[Gold]].}} {{TS|negative||Lose {{R|Golden Idol}}.}}\n* If the player lacks {{R|Golden Idol}}, this option is replaced with {{Frame|Locked}} Requires: {{R|Golden Idol}}.\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n<br>\n<br>\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou stumble across something that feels * very* out of place. Before you, an enormous stony head emerges from a large wall segment that does not shift and change like the rest of this area.<br>\nThe head's mouth is wide open, and it reveals large intimidating teeth stained red with blood. The surface of the status is riddled with pictographs that seem to indicate people throwing themselves into the mouth of this head and being devoured. Why would anyone do that?\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Jump Inside}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAt first when you step into the mouth of the statue, nothing happens.<br>\nAs you start to feel more than a little foolish, the huge molars slam down from above, crushing you whole.<br>\n{{TS||shake|Darkness.}}<br>\nSometime later from within the dark, you see a sliver of light, and hear what you now realize is the sound of stony teeth slowly rising upwards.<br>\n<br>\n<br>\nYou leave confused.\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Offer: {{R|Golden Idol}}}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou jump back a little as the gigantic molars smash down on the idol, smashing it to dust. As the teeth start to rise up again, {{TS|gold||gold}} pours forth in a torrent from the opening, flooding you with riches.\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou leave, wondering what could have been.\n</div> </blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Golden Idol}} is acquired from the [[Act 1]] event of the same name; {{E|Golden Idol}}.\n* {{E|The Moai Head}} is the last opportunity to trade the {{R|Golden Idol}}, the other being the {{E|Forgotten Altar}} event in [[Act 2]].\n* The 333 [[Gold]] from {{Frame|Offer: Golden Idol}} easily outperforms any remaining [[Gold]] the player could gain from combats by keeping the {{R|Golden Idol}}, especially since they likely do not have many combats left in the run by the time they reach this [[Act 3]] event.\n* The healing from {{Frame|Jump Inside}} will be prevented if the player has {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The real world [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moai Moai] are a set of stone human-like statues constructed by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapa_Nui_people Rapa Nui people] on [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter_Island Rapa Nui (commonly known as Easter Island)].\n* This event may be a reference to the [https://spelunky.fandom.com/wiki/Moai_(HD) Moai from Spelunky], where they are a key component in accessing the City of Gold by entering the Moai's mouth.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Fixed an incorrect interaction with the Mark of the Bloom and the Moai Head event in Act 3.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3178":{"pageid":3178,"ns":0,"title":"The Ssssserpent","revisions":[{"revid":54558,"parentid":35661,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Ssssserpent\n|Image=Event-Serpent.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Doubt}}\n{{E|The Ssssserpent}} is an [[Event]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Agree}} {{TS|positive||Gain 175}} {{Asc|15|(150)}} {{TS|positive||Gold.}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Doubt}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Disagree}} Nothing happens.\n<br><br>\nYou are then given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou walk into a room to find a large hole in the ground. As you approach the hole, an enormous serpent creature appears from within.\n<br>\n{{TS||up|\"Ho hooo! Hello hello! what have we got here?}} Hello adventurer, I ask a simple question.\n<br>\nThe most fulfilling of lives is that in which you can {{TS|gold|up|buy anything!}}\n<br>\nDo you agree?\"\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Agree}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Yeeeeeeesssssssssssessss!\n<br>\nThissss will all be worthhh it.\n<br>\n..ssSSs..... ss... sssss....!\"}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe serpent rears its head and blasts a stream of {{TS|gold||gold}} upwards!\n<br>\nIt is amazing and terrifying simultaneously.\n<br>\nYou gather all the {{TS|gold||gold,}} thank the snake, and get going.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Disagree}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe serpent stares at you with a look of extreme disappointment.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Ssserpent Head}} from the {{E|Face Trader}} event references this event. There is no special dialogue if the player encounters {{E|The Ssssserpent}} while owning their face.\n* The internal name of this event is <code>Liars_Game</code>.\n** This is a reference to the manga [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liar_Game ''Liar Game''], as confirmed by one of the developers on Discord<ref>https://ptb.discord.com/channels/309399445785673728/309399445785673728/780191500973375488</ref>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient SFX for Sssserpent event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Fixed typo in Sssserpent event text.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** The Serpent's offer is now more compelling.\n<br>\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3069":{"pageid":3069,"ns":0,"title":"We Meet Again!","revisions":[{"revid":54548,"parentid":35698,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=We Meet Again!\n|Image=Event-WeMeetAgain.png\n}}\n{{E|We Meet Again!}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Give Potion}} {{TS|negative||Lose a chosen potion.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a Relic.}}\n* The event will randomly choose a potion upon entry and tell you which one was selected. You will be unable to drink or discard that potion until you leave the event's floor.\n\n{{Frame|Give Gold}} {{TS|negative||Lose Gold.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a Relic.}}\n* The amount of [[Gold]] lost is between 50 and 150 (or your current amount of [[Gold]]).\n\n{{Frame|Give Card}} {{TS|negative||Lose a chosen card.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a Relic.}}\n* The chosen card will not be {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} or a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n\n{{Frame|Attack}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"We meet again!\" <br>\nA cheery disheveled fellow approaches you gleefully. You do not know this man. <br>\n\n\"It's me! {{TS|gold||Ranwid!}} Have any goods for me today? The usual? A fella like me can't make it alone, you know?\" <br>\nYou eye him suspiciously and consider your options.\n</div>\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Give Potion}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Exquisite! Was feeling parched.\" <br>\n{{TS|blue|up|Glup glup glup}} <br>\n\nHe downs the potion in one go and lets out a satisfied {{TS||shake|burp.}} <br>\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Give Gold}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Magnificent! This will be quite handy if I run into those {{TS|red||mask wearing hoodlums}} again.\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Give Card}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Exemplary! I shall study this further in my chambers.\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">He rummages around in his various pockets... <br>\n\"Here, look what I've got for you today! Take it take it!\"</div>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Attack}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"{{TS||shake|Aaaaagghh!!}} What a jerk you are sometimes!\" <br>\nHe runs away.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* \"{{TS|red||mask wearing hoodlums}}\" likely refers to the group of bandits in the Act 2 event {{E|Masked Bandits}}.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3176":{"pageid":3176,"ns":0,"title":"Wing Statue","revisions":[{"revid":55607,"parentid":54559,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Wing Statue\n|Image=Event-WingStatue.png\n}}\n{{E|Wing Statue}} is an [[Event]] found in [[Act 1]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 7 HP.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Destroy}} {{TS|positive||Receive 50 - 80 Gold.}}\n* Requires an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card in the player's deck that deals 10 or more damage '''in a single hit''' (e.g. {{C|Twin Strike}} does not count).\n* If the player's deck does satisfy the condition, this option is replaced with {{Frame|Locked}} Requires: Card with 10 or more damage.\n* See the [[#Notes|Notes]] section for more details on which cards satisfy this requirement.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n<br>\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>Among the stone and boulders, you notice an intricate large blue statue resembling a wing.</i><br>\n<i>You find {{TS|gold||gold}} spilling from its cracks. Maybe there is more inside...</i><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>Someone once told you of a cult that worshipped a giant bird. As you kneel in prayer, you begin to {{TS||up|feel}} ... {{TS||up|lightheaded}} .</i><br> <!-- Yes, there is actually a space between \"lightheaded\" and the period in the event text -->\n<i>You wake up some time later, feeling strangely fleet of foot.</i><br><br>\n{{Frame|Continue}} Opens the player's deck and has them select a card to remove.\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Destroy}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>With all your might, you hack away at the statue.</i><br>\n<i>It soon {{TS||shake|crumbles,}} revealing a {{TS|gold||pile of gold.}} You grab as much as you can and continue onwards.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>The statue makes you feel {{TS||up|uneasy.}} You walk past and continue onward.</i>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\nThe event specifically only checks {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack cards}} in the player's deck, despite only stating \"Cards\" in general. It also only checks whether the card's ''base damage'' is 10 or more. This means that any card that can only achieve 10 or more damage through the use of multi-hits (such as {{C|Twin Strike}} and {{C|Riddle with Holes}}) or that have damage which is dynamically calculated from certain conditions in combat (such as {{C|Perfected Strike}} and {{C|Mind Blast}}) do not meet the requirement.\n\n=== Cards With 10 or More Damage ===\nThe following is a list of cards that satisfy the condition of '''\"Requires: Card with 10 or more damage.\"''' for the {{Frame|Destroy}} option:\n* {{C|Clash}}\n* {{C|Clothesline}}\n* {{C|Heavy Blade}}\n* {{C|Wild Strike}}\n* {{C|Blood for Blood}}\n* {{C|Carnage}}\n* {{C|Hemokinesis}}\n* {{C|Searing Blow}}\n* {{C|Sever Soul}}\n* {{C|Uppercut}}\n* {{C|Bludgeon}}\n* {{C|Feed}}\n* {{C|Immolate}}\n* {{C|Bane}}\n* {{C|Flying Knee}}\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}}\n* {{C|All-Out Attack}}\n* {{C|Backstab}}\n* {{C|Choke}}\n* {{C|Dash}}\n* {{C|Masterful Stab}}\n* {{C|Predator}}\n* {{C|Die Die Die}}\n* {{C|Grand Finale}}\n* {{C|Unload}}\n* {{C|Streamline}}\n* {{C|Doom and Gloom}}\n* {{C|Melter}}\n* {{C|Sunder}}\n* {{C|All for One}}\n* {{C|Core Surge}}\n* {{C|Hyperbeam}}\n* {{C|Meteor Strike}}\n* {{C|Conclude}}\n* {{C|Reach Heaven}}\n* {{C|Sands of Time}}\n* {{C|Signature Move}}\n* {{C|Wheel Kick}}\n* {{C|Brilliance}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n* {{C|Hand of Greed}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n\n=== Cards With 10 or More Damage After Being Upgraded ===\nThe following is a list of cards that satisfy the condition of '''\"Requires: Card with 10 or more damage.\"''' for the {{Frame|Destroy}} option only after they have been [[Upgrade|Upgraded]] to increase their base damage:\n* {{C|Bash}}\n* {{C|Cleave}}\n* {{C|Headbutt}}\n* {{C|Pommel Strike}}\n* {{C|Reckless Charge}}\n* {{C|Fiend Fire}}\n* {{C|Dagger Throw}}\n* {{C|Quick Slash}}\n* {{C|Skewer}}\n* {{C|Glass Knife}}\n* {{C|Ball Lightning}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}}\n* {{C|Rebound}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}}\n* {{C|Scrape}}\n* {{C|Bowling Bash}}\n* {{C|Crush Joints}}\n* {{C|Empty Fist}}\n* {{C|Follow-Up}}\n* {{C|Sash Whip}}\n* {{C|Carve Reality}}\n* {{C|Fear No Evil}}\n* {{C|Wallop}}\n* {{C|Windmill Strike}}\n* {{C|Dramatic Entrance}}\n* {{C|Swift Strike}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Seeds are now utilized for Wing Statue event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Fixed a hyphen not being green for the Golden Wing event.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Fixed typo for Golden Wing locked option.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The internal name of this event is <code>Golden_Wing</code>.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3166":{"pageid":3166,"ns":0,"title":"World of Goop","revisions":[{"revid":54560,"parentid":35664,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=World of Goop\n|Image=Event-Goop.png\n}}\n{{E|World of Goop}} is an [[Event]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Gather Gold}} {{TS|positive||Gain 75 Gold.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 11 HP.}}\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Leave It}} {{TS|negative||Lose X Gold.}}\n* X is a random number between 20 and 50 {{Asc|15|(35 and 75)}} Gold. X cannot be more Gold than the player currently has.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou fall into a puddle.\n<br>\n{{TS||shake|IT'S MADE OF}} {{TS|green|shake|SLIME GOOP!!}}\n<br>\nFrantically, you claw yourself out over several minutes as you feel the goop starting to burn.\n<br>\nYou can feel goop in your ears, goop in your nose, goop everywhere.\n<br><br>\nClimbing out, you notice that some of your {{TS|gold||gold}} is missing. Looking back to the puddle you see your missing coins combined with {{TS|gold||gold}} from unfortunate adventurers mixed together in the puddle.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Gather Gold}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nFeeling the sting of the goop as the prolonged exposure starts to melt away at your skin, you manage to fish out the {{TS|gold||gold.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave It}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou decide that mess is not worth it.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The name \"World of Goop\" is a reference to the puzzle game [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_of_Goo World of Goo].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Goop Puddle event slightly reworked to be more interesting.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]}}}}